10 An act relating to establishing the Vermont Prescription Drug Discount
11 Card Program
12 It is hereby enacted by the General Assembly of the State of Vermont:
13 Sec. 1. 18 V.S.A. chapter 91, subchapter 7 is added to read:
14 Subchapter 7. Vermont Prescription Drug Discount Card Program
15 § 4691. VERMONT PRESCRIPTION DRUG DISCOUNT CARD
16 PROGRAM
17 (a) There is established the Vermont Prescription Drug Discount Card
18 Program, administered by the Office of the State Treasurer, for the purpose of
19 pooling prescription drug purchasing power with other U.S. states and

BILLAS PASSED BY THE HOUSE AND SENATE H.577
2026 Page 2 of 17
1 territories and nongovernmental organizations. The Program shall be made
2 available to all Vermont residents.
3 (b)(1) To further the purposes of the Program, the State Treasurer may
4 cooperate with other U.S. states and territories, regional consortia, or
5 nongovernmental organizations, or a combination of these, to pool prescription
6 drug purchasing power to:
7 (A) reduce prescription drug costs;
8 (B) negotiate discounts with prescription drug manufacturers;
9 (C) centralize prescription drug purchasing; and
10 (D) establish volume discount contracting.
11 (2) As used in subdivision (1)(D) of this subsection, “volume discount
12 contracting” means the negotiated purchase of a large quantity of a
13 prescription drug at a decreased cost.
14 (c) The Treasurer may require that reasonable fees be charged to defray
15 Program costs. Notwithstanding any provision of 32 V.S.A. § 603 to the
16 contrary, the amount and method of collection of any fee shall be determined
17 by the Treasurer based on actual costs.
18 (d) On or before January 15, 2028, and annually thereafter, the State
19 Treasurer shall submit a report to the House Committee on Health Care, the
20 Senate Committee on Health and Welfare, and the Governor detailing the
21 activities of the Program during the previous calendar year, including the

BILLAS PASSED BY THE HOUSE AND SENATE H.577
2026 Page 3 of 17
1 number of Vermont residents and pharmacies participating in the Program and
2 the amount of savings on prescription drug costs achieved.
3 § 4692. VERMONT PRESCRIPTION DRUG DISCOUNT CARD
4 PROGRAM FUND
5 (a) The Vermont Prescription Drug Discount Card Program Fund is
6 established as a special fund to be administered by the State Treasurer to
7 support the Vermont Prescription Drug Discount Card Program established in
8 this subchapter.
9 (b) The Fund shall consist of:
10 (1) any monies appropriated to the Fund by the General Assembly;
11 (2) any monies transferred to the Fund from the federal government,
12 other State agencies, or other government source;
13 (3) any monies from the payment of fees or other monies due to the
14 Program; and
15 (4) any gifts, grants, or donations made to the Fund and any gifts,
16 grants, donations, or investments received by the Treasurer for the Program.
17 (c) The Treasurer shall credit to the Fund all interest earned on Fund
18 balances and any other income derived from the deposit and investment of
19 monies in the Fund.
20 (d) Any unexpended and unencumbered monies in the Fund at the end of a
21 fiscal year shall remain in the Fund.

